# A small storyboard that renders anywhere the tool runs: every page, picture and command in it is in this repository,
# so it needs no network. Render it:
#
#     python scripts/video/render.py scripts/video/sample.storyboard
#
# The format is described at the top of storyboard.py. A scene is `--- name`, the words (`say:`), and one thing to show.

title: Sample storyboard
size: 1280x720
fps: 30
voice: piper:en_US-lessac-medium
cwd: ../..
env: PYTHONPATH=src

--- title
say: This is a sample of the video tool. A storyboard says what to show and what to say. A voice, a browser and ffmpeg
  make the video with no one at the keyboard.
show: still sample/card.svg
hold: 5

--- page
say: A scene can show a real page. This one is a file in the repository; an address on the web works the same way.
  The page scrolls while the words are spoken.
show: url sample/page.html
scroll: 1400
wait: 0.5

--- commands
say: Or it can show the real output of commands. They run once, when the video is made, and the terminal page replays
  what they printed, with the exit status and the time they took.
run: {python} scripts/deploy_v2.py hash tests/fixtures/knos_pay_v2_nodevnet.so
run: {python} -c "from knos.settle.v2 import pay; print('fee on a 20 USDC bounty:', pay.fee_of(20_000_000) / 1e6, 'USDC')"

--- close
say: The result is an H.264 file at a constant frame rate, a subtitle file, and a failure if the video is longer than
  three minutes.
show: still sample/end.svg
